---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../config/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Editorial Policy', url: '/editorial-policy/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial & Date Verification Policy | IndianTimers"
  description="Our rigorous methodology for verifying examination schedules, conducting primary authority audits, and maintaining zero-speculation countdown integrity."
  canonicalUrl={`${siteConfig.url}/editorial-policy/`}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
    <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">
        Editorial & Schedule Verification Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
        The standards and verification protocols governing all examination data on IndianTimers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">1. Primary Authority Sourcing Only</h2>
      <p>
        We strictly source examination schedules from primary, legally recognized conducting bodies:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-slate-500 pl-2">
        <li><strong>NTA (National Testing Agency)</strong>: exams.nta.ac.in & jeemain.nta.nic.in</li>
        <li><strong>UPSC</strong>: upsc.gov.in official gazette & annual calendars</li>
        <li><strong>IIT Joint Admission Boards</strong>: official organising institute portals</li>
        <li><strong>CBSE & State School Education Boards</strong>: official state government portals</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Secondary news aggregators, speculative blog posts, or social media rumors are never accepted as valid source citations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">2. The Four-Tier Status Classification</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-900/60 bg-emerald-50/50 dark:bg-emerald-950/20">
          <strong class="text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 block mb-0.5">Official Confirmed</strong>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">The conducting body has released a formal press circular or information bulletin with exact dates. Every such record links directly to the supporting official portal.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-900/60 bg-amber-50/50 dark:bg-amber-950/20">
          <strong class="text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300 block mb-0.5">Tentative (Official Calendar)</strong>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Published in an official annual programme (e.g. UPSC Annual Calendar) where the conducting body notes the dates are provisional and subject to change. Clearly labelled "Tentative" in the UI.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 block mb-0.5">Date Not Announced (TBA)</strong>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">If the official notification has not yet been released, the countdown badge displays "Date Not Announced". We refuse to invent speculative countdowns.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">3. Resolving Conflicting Information</h2>
      <p>
        When unofficial reports conflict with official gazettes, we prioritize the latest signed notice by the competent authority. In the rare event that an examination is postponed or rescheduled, the status is immediately flagged as <strong>Postponed / Rescheduled</strong> with the official postponement order number cited in the verification notes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">4. Transparent Verification Timestamps</h2>
      <p>
        Every examination record in our system maintains an auditable <code>lastVerified</code> ISO date. Routine audits run continuously to ensure dates stay in sync with the conducting authorities' portals.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">5. Corrections & Schedule Inquiries</h2>
      <p>
        If you identify an updated circular or discrepancy in any countdown schedule, please alert our editorial verification desk immediately at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`} class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold hover:underline">
          {siteConfig.contactEmail}
        </a>{' '}
        with the supporting official link or PDF.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
